00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.789 align:start position:0%
 
this week on indiana jones  damn it lovecraft country is back with  an adventure filled episode and there's  a ton to break down  in this video we'll be explaining some  of the episode's biggest wtf moments  including those underground tunnels the  introduction of yahima  and that crazy twist ending but before  we begin make sure to like and subscribe  so you're notified as soon as one of my  lovecraft breakdowns drops  well didn't take long for montrose to  hit the bottle in a recreation of what  is basically my friday night now there  are a bunch of  really cool clues here like how the  radio in the background talks about the  cold war claiming the americans are the  civilized ones in comparison to the  soviets this civilized versus savage  dichotomy is echoed in the museum when  one of the tour guides in the background  talks about  titus braithwick being civilized while  the natives he met were savages the  irony here being that titus was the  biggest savage of them all  the most important thing about this  scene however is that montrose says the  order of ancient dawn's book of law  and precepts which george gave him  before his death a book we saw george  pick up in a mysterious library in artem  in episode 2.  the book depicts a chronological history  of adam eve and  monsters this order is how montrose  atticus and letty are able to decipher  the door  leading to the vault later in the  episode but montrose ends up burning the  book even though in the voice over we  hear  george task montrose with giving that  book to atticus to quote  protect our family instead montrose  burns it even saying it smells like  tulsa which is a reference to the tulsa  race riots which both montrose and  george were a part of  christina arrives at letty's house  telling her that atticus tried to kill  her it seems she's been able to harness  the spell of invulnerability just like  her father  samuel last episode she said members of  the order are lucky if they can  harness one spell in their entire life  but it seems christina has mastered  several making her extremely powerful  but she's really here to retrieve  hiram's orry the mechanical model of a  solar system hippolyta was drawn to last  episode when she tries to get in she's  stopped by a force field now we aren't  sure how this force field came to be  was it some other magical force or was  it the witch doctor's magical protection  from last episode to ward off evil  spirits that's still holding  we even see the blood on the doorway  from that protection spell the ory isn't  here however hippolyta has taken it to  george's shop where she talks to her  father asking  which galaxy can sustain two sons like  this machine has  unfortunately it's broken and she can't  figure out how to get to the gears since  it's locked  a particular note here dee's friend bobo  bobo was emmett till's nickname now if  you don't know who emmett till is make  sure to check out my episode 3 breakdown  it seems his friendship with d  will play a larger role going forward as  episode 8 of this season  is apparently titled jigabobo lety finds  atticus at the colored-only library  researching about all the mysterious  things that have been going on but as  i'll find out his father has basically  taken out all the same books and knows a  heck of a lot more than he's letting on  atticus tells her that he's looking for  clues on titus braithwight's vault which  contains a set of deciphered pages from  the book of names  if he can get those pages maybe he can  start using spells to protect his family  also fun easter egg this little boy here  is reading journey to the center of the  earth which atticus makes reference to  when they later  journey into the center of the earth  type [ __ ] lydian atticus try to convince  montrose to tell them where this  vault is but he doesn't want them to get  themselves killed montrose however does  blurt out an interesting piece of  information here that there are  34 other lodges of the order of ancient  dawn christina plays hide and seek with  a bunch of kids i  found this such an odd thing for her to  be doing but she says she's never played  before perhaps hinting at a sheltered  childhood those of you with a keen eye  will see the  cops who come to pick her up here are  the same racist cops that drove past  letty's home in  episode 3. she's taken to captain  lancaster who we were also introduced to  last episode he says he runs this lodge  of the order in chicago and is curious  why she's come to his territory  unannounced apparently hiram's orary is  the key to unlocking titus braithwight's  time machine  and that's why she's here there's also  this weird moaning man locked away  we're unsure if lancaster just likes to  beat people up and block them away  or if this is some important character  we'll see in future episodes regardless  christina is told to know her place  since she's a woman  and women aren't even allowed in the  order this will likely just  fuel her even more the group is off to  boston on a secret trip to find the  vault disguised as a trip to the  astronomy museum meanwhile rose is off  to apply for a job at marshall's  something she told ledy she wanted to do  in previous episodes but when she gets  there she finds another black woman  already working there essentially making  it impossible for her to land the job  as she tells william later on they'll  never hire more than two black women  back at the museum tree who's on his way  to philly and hitched a ride with the  group  alludes to atticus that montrose is gay  saying that since he left him and sammy  the guy in episode 1 who was caught in  the alleyway with another man  had been getting close if this is true  it would explain a lot more about  montrose's wife hooking up with george  and if i'm going to be honest this seems  to be the only reason why the writers  put tree on this trip  to give that bit of info so it's likely  true  william ends up beating the crap out of  two men tasked with following christina  he tells them he has a date tonight  which we'll find out is with ruby  they hook up and she seems to be totally  cool with the fact he has this satanic  like scar on his chest with ruby pissed  at letty for not telling her about her  mother's secret inheritance which was  actually just money given by christina  this is likely all an elaborate plan to  use ruby  and gain access to the house and the  orrery atticus letty and montrose gain  access to titus braythright's wing at  night  finding a hidden vault underneath the  statue one which leads to a series of  tunnels each path relates to one of  titus's expeditions and i have to be  honest with you i've re-watched this  scene multiple times and i'm still  confused how they knew which path to go  down it has something to do with an  expedition to guyana a renovation to the  museum  but they end up taking the north path  even though guyana would be south of  boston  if you got this part please let me know  in the comments because i was like  ladies first as letty is the first to  traverse the plank over this  giant chasm when it starts to magically  disintegrate they have mere moments to  input the correct order on this vault  door  only to find in the next section they're  racing against time as the tide rises  there's this interesting moment between  atticus and montrose where atticus gets  triggered when he's accused of quote  leaving men behind he says he's never  left a man behind referring to his time  in the korean war but it seems like he  has left a woman behind we haven't  really met gi yet the mysterious korean  he called in episode 1  but expect her to play a bigger role in  episodes to come  atticus also learns that montrose burned  the order's book in an effort to protect  them this is an important note in  figuring out this  episode's twist ending letty finds the  body of one of her neighbors floating in  the tunnel one of the dudes who died by  the ghost  last episode and whose body was left  beneath the winthrop home not only that  but the tunnel links to her home  hundreds of miles away in chicago it  seems these tunnels don't abide by the  rules of space and time heck we just saw  a plank  magically disintegrate this makes me  extremely curious what the other paths  could lead to  other locations or other times after  atticus and mantras have their first  actual father-son heart to heart they  come across a door with a severed arm  it seems as though only those with  titus's bloodline can unlock it and  fortunately for atticus he's got that  covered inside they find titus's  exploration ship and several decaying  bodies  among them holding the deciphered pages  is a two-spirit named yahima one who  possesses the genitalia of both a man  and a woman  she speaks arawak a language of the  indigenous people of south america and  the caribbean  and she tells them that titus imprisoned  her on his ship  and killed her family somehow atticus  understands her language  yahima has the ability to decipher the  book of names something she knows by  having studied the symbols from the cave  of  alamun kundi now i searched aliban kundi  and  nothing came up so it's likely this was  created for the show  however it's uncertain if we'll ever  visit it or if it will be a larger plot  point in the future  montrose takes the pages which causes  the ship to basically  self-destruct and they make their way  back up the elevator to letty's house  taking yahima with them but when she  opens her mouth she lets out  a wailing scream which atticus has to  knock her out just to make it stop  that's because yahima is a siren cursed  by titus so she can't speak  should she ever escape the vault  meanwhile d and hippolyta are on their  way back home after having found out the  group had somehow already made it back  to chicago  she finds dee looking at george's atlas  which was in the glove compartment an  atlas which shows where he was actually  going during the trip  which took his life you'll see here that  devon county is circle the place where  artem is located  and hippolyta turns the car around  likely headed there  in her search for answers atticus tells  montrose that yahima doesn't think she  can break her siren spell but in the  meantime atticus has those pages and  hopes he can figure them out  and they share a poignant moment  montrose even saying  you grew to be a good man in spite of me  this happens mere moments before he  ventures into yahima's room  and slits her throat there has been some  discussion if this is even montrose and  i do think it is  he even says i'm sorry to her before he  does it there's still a semblance of  humanity here but every action montrose  has taken this episode has been for the  protection of his son  so this has got to be one too right we  also know that montrose knows a lot more  than he's leading on  there's something he knows about her and  this whole mystery that we  don't yet something so dangerous he must  kill her in order to protect  everyone just what that is we'll have to  wait and find  out thanks again for watching everyone  please make sure to like and subscribe  and for more bat takes you can always  follow me on twitter at thingstoryt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much

